  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Long pass, round the cone and shoot",
  "description": "Two queues, A on the left and C on the right, at the centre line. Two passers, B and D, stand far up near the end line, one on each side. One cone per side a little outside the penalty area, and a goalkeeper in goal.\n\nA skates off with the ball and, on the move, plays a long pass diagonally across the rink to B. A carries on to the cone, rounds it, and B plays the ball back so A can take it at speed and shoot from distance – the shot should come from outside the penalty spot. Then C starts and plays the same with D. The two sides alternate.\n\nAfter the shot, A and C swap queues. B and D are replaced when the coach says so. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Have speed on your skates already when you play the long pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The long pass should be firm and along the ice, straight onto the passer's stick."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The passer plays the return in front of the shooter, not at them."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Shoot from outside the penalty spot – the long-range shot is what we train."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "main",
  "difficulty": 3,
  "focus": [
